REScue bundles two third-party datasets, merged into one file (src/data/neutrality-scores.json,
used by the neutrality filter):

- News Sharing on Social Media: Mapping the Ideology of News Media, Politicians, and the Mass Public
  Gregory Eady, Richard Bonneau, Joshua A. Tucker and Jonathan Nagler.
  Political Analysis 33(2), 2025, doi:10.1017/pan.2024.19. Replication data on Harvard Dataverse,
  doi:10.7910/DVN/1QMLOV, file News_Domain_Media_Scores.csv. Licence: CC0 1.0.
  Only the "domain" and "zeta" columns are used. Scores for about 180 major outlets, from
  politicians' news sharing 2017-2020, are mapped onto the scale below with a linear fit and
  replace the 2018 scores for those domains.

- Partisan Bias Scores for Web Domains (2018)
  Ronald E. Robertson, Shan Jiang, Kenneth Joseph, Lisa Friedland, David Lazer and Christo Wilson.
  Harvard Dataverse, doi:10.7910/DVN/QAN5VX, file 3316961 (bias_scores.tab). Licence: CC0 1.0.
  Only the "domain" and "score" columns are used. The score is the authors' audience-partisanship
  measure from a 2017 Twitter panel: it shows who shares a domain, not a judgement of its content.
  Regenerate with: node --experimental-strip-types scripts/build-neutrality-data.ts [bias_scores.tab] [News_Domain_Media_Scores.csv]
